4} {:answer/id #uuid "54b76232-1674-5242-9acf-123f7bdcf11e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<y<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401115} {:answer/id #uuid "3512bb23-ec85-559a-bb44-2c0d0c3ebdfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le y\\le 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54b76232-1674-5242-9acf-123f7bdcf11e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<y<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401115} :answer-field/id #uuid "071a160d-4402-56e8-b9f3-e34425bb2388" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "846d6059-ad4f-5e01-8a65-610c7d23e3a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-158314" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b95c538613ee8672e0f1cac970b7af230ec40bf3075e609b1e03f7cad4382fb1.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<1,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/19/19e8e52881066864cba562ed2a8cdc2944b9dae416c7124fdee207cdad1d8bdf.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/90/907e996fb7aea36e0c924feb0f5d9dc6804c768be775953d277e84b0145ef5a0.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<1,\\,-1<y<0}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6df4c2be-04e6-571f-b0a9-dfab0dd98141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448466} {:answer/id #uuid "6e49a39a-5368-5de8-8c63-144924ac30d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e49a39a-5368-5de8-8c63-144924ac30d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448467} :answer-field/id #uuid "efee37f6-b4c6-545d-bd91-c2a4f79965cc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449273} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a00d201-d27c-52d0-8af0-2805fae6cd94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448468} {:answer/id #uuid "75d7e2d1-7f56-515b-bd02-787ded8e5270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75d7e2d1-7f56-515b-bd02-787ded8e5270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448469} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2b89ba2-4284-58ef-a934-c6ed5ebe6b7d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449274} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c6ba7f9-51b0-5600-a4ea-f1ca0eedcc9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448470} {:answer/id #uuid "8af85e9b-1a4d-52a0-b5dc-188c47bd77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8af85e9b-1a4d-52a0-b5dc-188c47bd77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448471} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4439f51-b7e9-58c6-8132-dce6ead75ac7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "68256c62-7faf-5747-9e8c-b2c67a0a95a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-161444" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n\n- **II.** $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n\n- **III.** $∂A⊂A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/62/62c410c21e79e1bc688c1ff1a3440a207c62bcad42525bdc93fa2770b76d48bd.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/33/33a4738b642443c2535d347aa53ee2b7b80c800142c4844d94578769118ebfbc.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points, so we must have $∂A⊂A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e10af6b-0591-5053-99a4-daa139c38eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>-1+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378845} {:answer/id #uuid "6db4587d-cb4b-5833-8c4e-4aaa4bbaceb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<-1+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378846} {:answer/id #uuid "0010883b-56fc-5f98-bf3b-0ca63324c983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378847} {:answer/id #uuid "f36ec4d6-3398-59fb-96fa-76646653031c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\ge -1+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378848} {:answer/id #uuid "a21a36f6-b572-588d-aa2e-573d52ea0330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le -1+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0010883b-56fc-5f98-bf3b-0ca63324c983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378847} :answer-field/id #uuid "59c8bfe0-08bc-5e9b-93ce-301d8e63019e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4a26d47e-204e-5e18-9063-2683b6b0394d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161593" :question/problem "![](images/80/80bde6a20ceed7c052a87eda6f05c542f6046de7014f6402f5f453b6610f8d42.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05b25521109f373e2a7718523ce6289b27b37bd185d4fc60f0d052c232f4f8a4.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=-1+x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=-1+x\\,}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5b39a98-ac20-5cbf-805a-5c64b48f4d91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449958} {:answer/id #uuid "a6123e03-9f1a-55ae-8049-e66f7df48abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6123e03-9f1a-55ae-8049-e66f7df48abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449959} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb5b9ea3-b19f-572e-90a5-93f3f3d18280" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc09b043-a237-5147-8e74-3cb2d48c0db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449960} {:answer/id #uuid "d3f5341e-9ebd-53a8-b977-c25f8d8c2d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc09b043-a237-5147-8e74-3cb2d48c0db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449960} :answer-field/id #uuid "45b72198-7edb-5c3f-a56e-f84b68b732be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450934} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e755d2a-b5e6-5e96-88fd-d0e6cd0cfc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449962} {:answer/id #uuid "896e016a-452b-53dc-9c84-3690b98756c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "896e016a-452b-53dc-9c84-3690b98756c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449963} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b80112e-c8cb-5761-852a-1dc1da395e6b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "baee2889-195d-5ff5-b660-0a9acac1604c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161626" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- **II.** $A-\\text{int}\\,A=∂A$\n- **III.** $∂A⊂{R}^{2}-A$" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/45/4540e03fc5404474a0cd900c89004e6a5cfe7ac2d4702348e9d0395fc1c914e9.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.  \n\n![](images/2a/2a93b912f0d7b3a84bf0ec9c3b3596d080a9e71a345ff436e2f591edf042d9db.png)\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $A=\\text{int}\\,A$ or, equivalently,  $A-\\text{int}\\,A=∅.$\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points, so we must have $∂A⊂{R}^{2}-A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and  III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f89386f9-8a2b-56eb-8521-7c1ddafcfd96" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Interior of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43574f05-777a-549d-bcc5-4111c8c8d7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279195} {:answer/id #uuid "5a9719d8-ee0b-5a00-a340-ff263989cce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\le y\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279427} {:answer/id #uuid "ca03051f-af96-56ae-ab61-1088cac3f4b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280361} {:answer/id #uuid "d49251f6-f1c4-5cb4-80d5-9e8219614615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280466} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf5aa37-a11b-5e7d-9327-c99e5e66d2dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\le y\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d49251f6-f1c4-5cb4-80d5-9e8219614615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<y<2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280466} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6060a7f-f5cd-551c-84e4-60b33ad6abe7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62cf2373-4936-5999-9138-7b1b78c43b9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161730" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa335a55f5b4496cdaccca5d35e286a168598761188bc520c81397ef136f927d.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/fb/fba9ba3e52ed19eb0bb2286ae59c49bb9dc648134d9eab3c4e2d13862963f736.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2f3cd30dbaa4f84c43f2a7f1197aa904e3d43b1212241ae26736b2a0087f6170.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2}.\n$$"}]}
